:false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"MikeWang is named top at 81.6%, within range. Mei Chen is credited with 9.7% and the Time7 accessor, and Ravi Menon is given only 1.9% (below the 5% limit). Ravi isn't credited with Mei's lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows database_sql.go, which was renamed from sql.go, and names Justin Overfelt as top with 39.6% (in range). Ravi holds 0 lines. However, it names only Justin and Paul as original authors, not Andrew Stone, David Wheeler or Daniel Souza. It does say that no one holding lines is active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Says 4 of 52 people are active and hold 4.3% of lines, which implies 95.7% are held by departed people (in range). But it recommends Ravi, Alexander Rowe and Mei Chen as the active holders, treats Mei as active, and says it did not merge Alex Rowe and Alexander Rowe. It also does not mention Kofi Mensah.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Does not name Noor Haddad or Sam Okafor as owners, and Sam is not credited with code. However, it does not discuss Kofi Mensah, the bot commits or the noise explicitly. It avoids the failure conditions but doesn't show the positive handling of Kofi's date.\",\"pass\":true}],\"B\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Uses commit counts instead of blame and gives no line shares. It says Paul Borman last committed 2021-07-12, which is wrong (2023). Its table lists Sam Okafor as the most recent commit on time.go because of the line-ending change. It does not give Paul's share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Names MikeWang as the original v7 author but gives no percentage. Mei Chen is not credited with the Time7 accessor or any lines, and Ravi Menon is called the newest maintainer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows history with --follow and names David E. Wheeler, Justin Overfelt and Andrew Stone as original authors who left. It gives no percentage and does not name Justin as the largest author. It also points to Ravi as the most recent maintainer of the SQL code, though not as its owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Says nobody has committed in the last 90 days, which is wrong because Ravi's commit is within the window. It does not give the share of lines owned by departed people, does not merge Alex Rowe, and does not mention Kofi Mensah.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Lists Sam Okafor in the activity list and as the last committer on time.go, though it identifies his commit as line-ending normalization. It doesn't name him an owner. But it doesn't address Noor Haddad, Kofi Mensah or the bots. It also asserts that nobody committed in 90 days, which is wrong for Kofi's Dec 2025 commit.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\": [{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Uses blame ignoring the line-ending commit and names Paul Borman as having the most lines, but gives no percentage. It lists Sam Okafor with about 18 lines in the table. It says Paul's last commit was 2016, which is wrong (2023), though it calls him unlikely to be active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Names MikeWang as having the most lines and credits Mei Chen with 11 lines and the Time7 accessor. Ravi Menon gets 2 lines (1.7%). No percentage is given for MikeWang, but the attributions are correct.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Names Justin Overfelt as having the most lines, with Andrew Stone and David Wheeler also listed but not Daniel Souza. It gives no percentage. Ravi is mentioned only as the one who renamed the file, not as an author. It also adds Bryan Matsuo and Paul Borman, which is a partial match.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Says it can't confirm who is still around, gives no share of lines owned by departed people, and treats Alexander Rowe separately, calling Ravi the only likely active person. It does not mention Kofi Mensah.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Does not credit Sam Okafor with real authorship, saying the line-ending commit is misleading. It lists him with about 18 lines in the table, though as an artifact. It doesn't mention Noor Haddad, Kofi or the bots. Sam is not named an expert, so it avoids the failure conditions.\",\"pass\":true}]}","ttft_ms":13122,"type":"result","duration_ms":13144,"uuid":"72d89097-ea98-4e22-8242-2ec27fbe00be","ttft_stream_ms":1823,"time_to_request_ms":407,"first_content_frame_ms":1823,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
